TheindexOf()method searches an array for an element value and returns its position.

Array.indexOf()returns -1 if the item is not found.

If the item is present more than once, it returns the position of the first 
occurrence.

Array.lastIndexOf()is the same asArray.indexOf(), but 
returns the position of the last occurrence of the specified element.

ECMAScript 2016 introducedArray.includes()to arrays.
This allows us to check if an element is present in an array (including NaN, unlike indexOf).

